But `MlKitTranslator` is referenced from the main source set (in `BootstrapManager`), so the class must exist at compile time. The cleanest solution: define `MlKitTranslator` as an interface in main, and provide the implementation only in the mlkit flavor.

### Restructure `MlKitTranslator` (main)

### `android/app/src/main/java/com/oarumi/app/data/mlkit/MlKitTranslator.kt`

```kotlin
package com.oarumi.app.data.mlkit

/**
 * Interface so the argos flavor can compile without the ML Kit dependency.
 * The mlkit flavor provides [RealMlKitTranslator]; the argos flavor provides
 * no binding (BootstrapManager receives null).
 */
interface MlKitTranslator {
    fun supportedLanguages(): Set<String>
    suspend fun isDownloaded(sourceLang: String): Boolean
    suspend fun ensureModel(sourceLang: String): Boolean
    suspend fun translate(text: String, sourceLang: String, offline: Boolean = false): String
    fun close()
}
